 "notes": "Region (Speyside, Highland, Islands, Islay, Lowland, Campbeltown) is a type, per the Scotch Whisky Association regions on the Scotch_whisky page. Old models that belong to a distillery archetype became its versions; the rest of the Scotch models stay in m (duplicates removed: second Manta Ray and second Rosebank listing, 3 extra Nc'nean, second Torabhaig, Loch Lomond Remarkable Alchemy, Darkness 8yo (no maker)). MOVE to the World/Irish/Japanese/American whisky shelves (not Scotch): Amrut Fusion; Kavalan Solist Vinho Barrique; Nikka Yoichi 10yo; Sakurao Togouchi; Starward Tawny; Sullivans Cove French Oak; Callington Mill PX; St George Baller; Stranahan's Snowflake; KI ONE Signature; Thy Whisky Casks 1035+1036; The English Distillery Sherry Hogshead; Teeling (4 listings), The Donn (Craft Irish Whiskey), Titanic Distillers 8 YO; Ichiro's Malt & Grain; Jameson Triple Triple; Midleton Very Rare 2026; Tullamore D.E.W. 12; Longleaf Cask Strength Heirloom; Kwun Cheung blended malt; Fercullen 15; Frey Ranch 100% Barley; Waterloo The Duke Rum Cask. Blend ranges in r kept only for houses without an archetype (Johnnie Walker, Chivas Regal, Ballantine's, Dewar's, Famous Grouse, Royal Salute, Haig ranges are now archetypes). No tradition entries: Scotch is an industrial-regional category, not an artisan craft tradition in the register's sense. Not added for want of a retrieved source: Compass Box archetype years, Great King Street/Asyla/Oak Cross, other single grains (Cameron Brig, Girvan, North British)."
